AGENTIC-003 — Authentication (S2-001)

Type: AGENT
Sprint: Sprint 2
Owner: Agent (Replit)
Governor: Alex (review on completion)
Status: Ready

🎯 Intent

Introduce minimal, boring, and safe authentication so users can return and retrieve what they were exploring — without introducing deal semantics, commitment signals, or UX drift.

Authentication in Sprint 2 exists only for identity continuity.

🧭 Product Context (Non-Negotiable)

FractPath is still a pre-deal exploration platform.

In Sprint 2:

Scenarios are non-binding

No deals exist

No property verification exists

No approvals, submissions, or commitments exist

Authentication must feel like:

“Remember me so I can pick this up later.”

Authentication must not feel like:

Applying

Getting approved

Starting a deal

Locking in terms

🔒 UX & Semantic Constraints (Hard Rules)

Authentication must:

Be email-based

Use a managed auth provider (Supabase / Clerk / Auth0 / equivalent)

Use default provider UX or a minimal wrapper

Support sign up, sign in, sign out, and password recovery

Preserve existing public functionality

Authentication must not:

Introduce profiles, roles, or permissions

Introduce deal language

Introduce property concepts

Introduce sharing or collaboration

Introduce custom password rules or recovery UX

Block scenario generation behind login

If unsure → do not add it.

🛠️ Implementation Scope
Required

Email + password authentication

Session persistence across refresh

Server-side access to authenticated user context

Logout capability

Provider-default password reset flow

Explicitly Out of Scope

MFA

Social login

User profiles

Settings pages

Role selection (buyer/seller/realtor)

Deal IDs

Scenario persistence (handled in S2-002)

🔀 Routing Rules

Public routes remain accessible without auth

Authentication is required only for:

scenario retrieval (future ticket)

scenario persistence (future ticket)

Do not gate the Scenario Builder yet.

✅ Acceptance Criteria (All Must Pass)

 User can sign up with email/password

 User can log in

 User can log out

 User can reset password via provider flow

 Session persists across page refresh

 Public Scenario Builder still works without auth

 No deal, approval, or commitment language introduced

 No new product objects created

📦 Deliverables (Keep This Tight)

When complete, report only:

Summary of what was added

Files changed

How to test authentication locally

Any risks or assumptions made

Do not include verbose logs unless something failed.

⚠️ Known Failure Modes (Avoid These)

Over-customizing auth UX

Adding “submit”, “apply”, or “get started” language

Adding roles or profile setup

Blocking exploration behind login

Any of the above is grounds for rejection.

🧠 Governor Review Gate

This ticket is not done until:

UX language is reviewed against the Sprint 2 UX Intent Doc

Auth feels like identity continuity, not commitment

